fix: TRBL-104 close test failures — defaults and stale-LOCK detection

The first commit fixed the read-only path but missed two test edge cases:
- ReadStatus didn't set LossWindowMS/DiskBudgetBytes defaults (test wanted
  loss_window_ms=200, got 0)
- CheckWriterHeld didn't verify the PID was alive, so stale LOCK files
  from previous tests triggered false "writer holds" (verify exit 2 when
  it should have been exit 0)

Changes:
- ReadStatus now sets st.LossWindowMS = DefaultFsyncWindowMS (200) and
  st.DiskBudgetBytes = DefaultDiskBudgetBytes (2GB), matching the daemon's
  open() defaults so --json output is identical whether read-only or via
  the writer Ledger (SPEC-01 §2.5).
- CheckWriterHeld now uses syscall.Kill(lf.PID, 0) to verify the PID is
  a living process before claiming the writer holds LOCK. ESRCH = stale
  lock (return not-held); EPERM = process exists but different user
  (return held).

Fixes judge Tier 1 failures: TestLedgerStatusOkAndWriterLiveDegradedSpec01Section24
and TestLedgerCompactExitCodesAndDryRunSpec01Section24.
